Test the buttons, not the section. Replace
  var setR = $('#set').getBoundingClientRect(); if (setR.top < innerHeight && setR.bottom > 77) {
with
  var barTop = bar.getBoundingClientRect().top, addsOn = $$('#set .row .add, #addall').some(function (b) { var r = b.getBoundingClientRect(); return r.bottom > 85 && r.top < barTop - 8; }); if (addsOn) {
and log the mode as 'none_adds_visible'. Then, in the dock only, when the set lies below the bar ($('#set').getBoundingClientRect().top > barTop), append '<div class="acts"><span></span><a href="#set" data-toset>See the set</a></div>'; the card's existing data-toset handler scrolls there and closes it.

Count the exits and the objection-handling taps.
